    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2X3TLoPAVzhYQ8BZsrhPaQY)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Order: independent; safe to merge anytime. Based on `main`.\n- Builds on #428 (heading tags at the top right of results), already merged: that behaviour is kept, entries still use `sp-see-also-view--entry`.\n- Open PRs checked (#439, #438, #421, #420, #419, #418, #415, #171, #125): none touches `sp-see-also`.\n- Branch name is not number-prefixed (the rename API is blocked here); retarget nothing, no other PR uses this branch as base.\n- After merging: nothing to retarget.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Problem:** `sp-see-also` (outgoing: what this litnote mentions) and `sp-see-also-show-concept` (incoming: who mentions a concept) were two separate views, and for a litnote you could not see all the ways it is referenced.\n- **One interface:** `sp-see-also-show &optional TARGET`, one buffer `*see-also*`.\n  - no argument: the litnote of the current buffer; `C-u`: pick any note by title; from Lisp, TARGET is nil, a file or a note ID.\n  - `sp-see-also-show-concept` and `-by-name` stay as thin wrappers, nothing breaks.\n- **Two parts in the view:**\n  - \"This note mentions\": concepts and open questions, as before (left out for a note with no file of its own).\n  - \"Referenced by\": every litnote that refers to the note, with a count per way, e.g. `×4 · footnote 1 · link 1 · parent 1 · cite 1`.\n- **Ways a note is referenced** (`sp-see-also-reference-kinds`, default all): `footnote`, `section`, `link` (any other `id:` link), `parent` (`parent ::` line), `cite` (citation of the note's `#+reference:` citekey).\n- New `sp-see-also-references ID CITEKEY EXCLUDE-FILE`; links, parent lines and citations are read from files each time, not cached (no cache version change). Source blocks and comments are ignored; the note's own file is left out.\n- Docs: `docs/tangles/academic/sp-see-also.org` (\"The two views\" rewritten as bullet lists, \"Using it\", Limits). Tangled `.el` and tests regenerated.\n- Tests: 41 ERT tests pass (6 new/changed) on Emacs 29.3; tangle check passes. `when-let*` style only. No CHANGELOG edit.\n- Not run in the real GUI, vault or `vulpea-db`.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Pull this branch, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`) (untested by Claude: GUI)\n- [ ] In a litnote with a `#+reference:` citekey: `M-x sp-see-also-show`: \"This note mentions\" and \"Referenced by\" both show (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] In \"Referenced by\", another note that cites the key, links its ID in prose, and has a `parent ::` line shows one entry per way with `[cite]`, `[link]`, `[parent]`\n- [ ] `C-u M-x sp-see-also-show`, pick a concept by title: same buffer, \"Referenced by\" lists its footnote mentions\n- [ ] `M-x sp-see-also-show-concept` on a heading with an ID, and `M-x sp-see-also-show-concept-by-name`: both still work\n- [ ] RET on a concept heading in the first part opens that concept's view\n- [ ] `(setq sp-see-also-reference-kinds '(footnote))`, `g`: only footnote entries remain\n- [ ] Edge: a note with no ID gives \"This note has no ID…\"; time the view on the real vault (all files are read when a citekey is set)\n- [ ] Regression: heading tags still sit at the right edge, `TAB`, `n`/`p` work; the sidebar `see-also` widget and `concept-usage` dblock are unchanged\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .` (`git clean -fd` only after checking `git clean -nd`).\n- Back to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`.\n- Optionally delete the test branch locally: `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D claude/project-thread-ljq060` (the remote copy stays until the PR is merged or closed).\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n- Nothing changes in the vault (the view only reads), so nothing to restore there.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiDKvUbMh4QJrqjE4tY)_",
